KeepVocab modifications: affine 4-bit token-embedding quantization in blocks of
64, stored as packed byte pairs and unpacked for requested tokens with standard
ONNX operators for WASM compatibility. The full 256,000-token vocabulary is
retained. Remaining text and vision weights use upstream q4f16 conversion.
The tokenizer is losslessly compressed for transport. Text transport shards
reconstruct one gzip stream; they are not separate encoders.

Reproduce with scripts/export-siglip2-compact.py. Exact lengths, provenance and
SHA-256 values are recorded in manifest.json. This is a modified, lossy-quantized
checkpoint, not a claim of identical outputs to the original model.
